    "summary": "Successfully implemented KIP-1319: Align TxnOffsetCommit API with OffsetCommit API.\n\n## Changes Made:\n\n### 1. TxnOffsetCommitRequest.java\n- Updated `getErrorResponseTopics()` to preserve topic IDs from request in error responses\n- Updated `getErrorResponse()` static method to include topic IDs in response data\n\n### 2. TxnOffsetCommitResponse.java\n- Changed `newBuilder()` to `newBuilder(boolean useTopicIds)` to support both topic ID and name modes\n- Updated abstract `Builder` class methods to accept `Uuid topicId` parameter:\n  - `get(Uuid topicId, String topicName)`\n  - `getOrCreate(Uuid topicId, String topicName)`\n  - `addPartition(Uuid topicId, String topicName, int partitionIndex, Errors error)`\n  - `addPartitions(Uuid topicId, String topicName, ...)`\n- Created `TopicIdBuilder` class for UUID-based topic indexing\n- Updated `TopicNameBuilder` to accept and preserve topic IDs\n\n### 3. Test Files\n- Updated TxnOffsetCommitRequestTest with topic ID support tests\n- Updated TxnOffsetCommitResponseTest with parameterized tests for both `useTopicIds=true` and `useTopicIds=false`\n\n## Test Results:\n✅ TxnOffsetCommitRequestTest: 36 tests passed\n✅ TxnOffsetCommitResponseTest: 14 tests passed\n✅ Total: 50 tests passed\n\nThe implementation aligns TxnOffsetCommit with OffsetCommit API by supporting both topic names and topic IDs, matching the pattern used in OffsetCommitResponse."
